      "text": "<think>\nI need to find the sum of 589,473,790 and 219,574,375.\n\nFirst, I'll add the two numbers together.\n\nAdding the units place: 0 + 5 = 5.\n\nNext, the tens place: 9 + 7 = 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1.\n\nThen, the hundreds place: 7 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1.\n\nContinuing this process for each digit place, I'll ensure that each addition accounts for any carry-over from the previous step.\n\nAfter adding all the digits, I'll combine the results to get the final sum.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of **589,473,790** and **219,574,375**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Write down the numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   &\\phantom{+}589,\\!473,\\!790 \\\\\n   +&\\phantom{+}219,\\!574,\\!375 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   &= \\,?\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Add the numbers digit by digit from right to left:**\n\n   - **Units place:**\n     \\[\n     0 + 5 = 5\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Tens place:**\n     \\[\n     9 + 7 = 16 \\quad \\text{(write down 6, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundreds place:**\n     \\[\n     7 + 3 + 1 = 11 \\quad \\text{(write down 1, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     3 + 4 + 1 = 8\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Ten-thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     7 + 7 = 14 \\quad \\text{(write down 4, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundred-thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     4 + 5 + 1 = 10 \\quad \\text{(write down 0, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Millions place:**\n     \\[\n     9 + 9 + 1 = 19 \\quad \\text{(write down 9, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Ten-millions place:**\n     \\[\n     8 + 1 + 1 = 10 \\quad \\text{(write down 0, carry over 1)}\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundred-millions place:**\n     \\[\n     5 + 2 + 1 = 8\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Billions place:**\n     \\[\n     6 + 1 = 7\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Ten-billions place:**\n     \\[\n     5 + 0 = 5\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundred-billions place:**\n     \\[\n     0 + 0 = 0\